.TH CHTTP_STATUS 3 "2026-07-14" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
CHTTP_STATUS_CONTINUE, CHTTP_STATUS_SWITCHING_PROTOCOLS, CHTTP_STATUS_OK, CHTTP_STATUS_CREATED, CHTTP_STATUS_ACCEPTED, CHTTP_STATUS_NO_CONTENT, CHTTP_STATUS_PARTIAL_CONTENT, CHTTP_STATUS_MOVED_PERMANENTLY, CHTTP_STATUS_FOUND, CHTTP_STATUS_NOT_MODIFIED, CHTTP_STATUS_TEMPORARY_REDIRECT, CHTTP_STATUS_PERMANENT_REDIRECT, CHTTP_STATUS_BAD_REQUEST, CHTTP_STATUS_UNAUTHORIZED, CHTTP_STATUS_FORBIDDEN, CHTTP_STATUS_NOT_FOUND, CHTTP_STATUS_METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED, CHTTP_STATUS_NOT_ACCEPTABLE, CHTTP_STATUS_REQUEST_TIMEOUT, CHTTP_STATUS_CONFLICT, CHTTP_STATUS_GONE, CHTTP_STATUS_PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE, CHTTP_STATUS_UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA, CHTTP_STATUS_UNPROCESSABLE, CHTTP_STATUS_TOO_MANY_REQUESTS, CHTTP_STATUS_INTERNAL_ERROR, CHTTP_STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED, CHTTP_STATUS_BAD_GATEWAY, CHTTP_STATUS_SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE, CHTTP_STATUS_GATEWAY_TIMEOUT, CHTTP_STATUS_HTTP_VERSION_NOT_SUPPORTED \- HTTP status code constants
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttp.h>

CHTTP_STATUS_CONTINUE               100
CHTTP_STATUS_SWITCHING_PROTOCOLS    101
CHTTP_STATUS_OK                     200
CHTTP_STATUS_CREATED                201
CHTTP_STATUS_ACCEPTED               202
CHTTP_STATUS_NO_CONTENT             204
CHTTP_STATUS_PARTIAL_CONTENT        206
CHTTP_STATUS_MOVED_PERMANENTLY      301
CHTTP_STATUS_FOUND                  302
CHTTP_STATUS_NOT_MODIFIED           304
CHTTP_STATUS_TEMPORARY_REDIRECT     307
CHTTP_STATUS_PERMANENT_REDIRECT     308
CHTTP_STATUS_BAD_REQUEST            400
CHTTP_STATUS_UNAUTHORIZED           401
CHTTP_STATUS_FORBIDDEN              403
CHTTP_STATUS_NOT_FOUND              404
CHTTP_STATUS_METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED     405
CHTTP_STATUS_NOT_ACCEPTABLE         406
CHTTP_STATUS_REQUEST_TIMEOUT        408
CHTTP_STATUS_CONFLICT               409
CHTTP_STATUS_GONE                   410
CHTTP_STATUS_PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE      413
CHTTP_STATUS_UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA      415
CHTTP_STATUS_UNPROCESSABLE          422
CHTTP_STATUS_TOO_MANY_REQUESTS      429
CHTTP_STATUS_INTERNAL_ERROR         500
CHTTP_STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED        501
CHTTP_STATUS_BAD_GATEWAY            502
CHTTP_STATUS_SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE    503
CHTTP_STATUS_GATEWAY_TIMEOUT        504
CHTTP_STATUS_HTTP_VERSION_NOT_SUPPORTED 505
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
These are integer constants for the common HTTP status codes. Use
these names instead of bare integer literals. Your code is then easier
to read.

This list does not hold every status code of the HTTP specifications.
It holds only the codes that the code and the test suites of this
library name. You can still use any other status code as a plain
integer literal with chttpsvr_resp_set_status(). You can also compare
any other status code directly against
chttpcli_response.status_code.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
if (resp->status_code == CHTTP_STATUS_NOT_FOUND) { ... }

chttpsvr_resp_set_status(resp, CHTTP_STATUS_SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpclient_do (3),
.BR chttpsvr_resp_set_status (3)
